post_install() {
    cat <<'EOF'
JetAutoClicker was installed.

For the global hotkey, add yourself to the "input" group (reading
/dev/input/event* is needed to detect the hotkey on Wayland):

    sudo usermod -aG input $USER

Then log out and back in.  On niri/sway the "Wayland virtual pointer" click
method needs no extra permissions.  The uinput fallback also needs write
access to /dev/uinput, which the installed udev rule grants to the "input"
group.

niri users may want to keep the window floating:
    window-rule {
        match app-id="jetautoclicker"
        open-floating true
    }
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    post_install
}
